Fine-tuning as "use" vs "derivative work"
-----------------------------------------
Following Creative Commons' May 2025 guidance "Using CC-licensed Works for
AI Training", CyberPuppy takes the interpretation that trained weights are
a "use" of the underlying datasets rather than a literal derivative work,
but nonetheless propagates the NonCommercial restriction because doing so
best respects the authors' stated intent. The ToxiCN NoDerivatives clause
is relaxed to ShareAlike (CC BY-NC-SA) to enable collaborative research
downstream; users requiring strict ND-compliance should not rely on
publicly-released CyberPuppy weights.

Takedown / dispute
------------------
If you are an author of any upstream dataset listed above and object to
this release, please open a discussion on the relevant Hugging Face repo
or email hctsai1006@cs.nctu.edu.tw. The artefacts will be removed or
relicensed within 7 days pending resolution.

